      },
      "description": "Counted once a viewer is actually subscribed, by the replica that owns its stream: a player that reached another pod is fetched from the owner and counts there, tagged relayed. Per attach rather than per connection, so a viewer held across a change of owner counts again - which is how often a stream moves under somebody watching. Mostly relayed means most viewers land on a replica that does not own their stream, which is a load-balancer question rather than a fault."
    },
    {
      "id": 25,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Viewers dropped for not reading",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "storage-demo-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
